From: Lukas Rieger <code@lukasrieger.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: refresh readiness when recreating an interface

After a power cycle the new supplicant interface can initially be disabled
by rfkill. Keeping interface_ready=true from the previous interface causes
interface_state() to skip finalize_interface_creation() when the new one
becomes ready. The device remains unpowered and scans fail with ENOLINK,
even though the WiFi technology reports Powered=true.

Always refresh the cached readiness from the newly created interface.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/plugins/wifi.c
+++ b/plugins/wifi.c
@@ -1559,8 +1559,8 @@
 	wifi->interface = interface;
 	g_supplicant_interface_set_data(interface, wifi);
 
-	if (g_supplicant_interface_get_ready(interface)) {
-		wifi->interface_ready = true;
+	wifi->interface_ready = g_supplicant_interface_get_ready(interface);
+	if (wifi->interface_ready) {
 		finalize_interface_creation(wifi);
 	}
 
